# Project Agent Instructions

Read and follow `WORKSPACE.md` first. Then read `AIWG.md` for AIWG discovery,
quick references, and framework routing.

Pi loads this file through its root-to-working-directory context chain. A nearer
`AGENTS.override.md` takes precedence, so keep project-specific overrides close
to the directory where they apply.

{{REMOTES_TOPOLOGY}}
## AIWG resources

- Shared Agent Skills are discovered from `.agents/skills/`.
- Pi prompt templates are discovered from `.pi/prompts/` and invoked as `/name`.
- Skills and prompt templates are distinct; invoke a skill as `/skill:name`.
- Project resources are trust-gated. Review them, then use `/trust` and restart
  Pi, or use `pi --approve` for a reviewed one-shot run.

Do not duplicate this context into `.pi/SYSTEM.md`; the canonical context is
`WORKSPACE.md`, `AIWG.md`, and this `AGENTS.md` bootstrap.
